=== Prompt ===
Who is Sherlock Holmes?

=== Response ===
Sherlock Holmes is a fictional detective created by British author Sir Arthur Conan Doyle. First appearing in the novel "A Study in Scarlet" in 1887, Holmes has since become one of the most famous and enduring characters in literature.

Holmes is known for his keen observational skills, logical reasoning, and expertise in criminal investigation. He often solves complex cases that stump other investigators, relying on his deductive abilities and knowledge of various sciences and arts to uncover the truth. His methods of detection include analyzing clues, interpreting footprints or handwriting, and understanding human behavior and psychology.

Holmes is also characterized by his sharp intellect, eccentric habits (such as his smoking of pipe tobacco and his interest in violin playing), and his occasional social awkwardness. He frequently collaborates with Dr. John Watson, a military doctor who serves as his trusted friend and chronicler.

The character of Sherlock Holmes has been adapted into numerous books, films, television series, and other media over the years, making him a beloved figure in popular culture.

